{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This quick start guide uses "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/stackotter\/swift-bundler","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Although not strictly required, it simplifies many aspects of cross-platform distribution and provides a platform-agnostic configuration format for specifying things such as app icons and custom URL schemes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you’re new to Swift, we recommend starting with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Setting-up-a-development-environment"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Installing-Swift-Bundler","type":"heading","text":"Installing Swift Bundler"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Follow ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/stackotter\/swift-bundler?tab=readme-ov-file#installation-","isActive":true},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mint"},{"text":" is the preferred installation method on macOS and Linux as of the last update to this quick start guide.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Installing-system-dependencies","type":"heading","text":"Installing system dependencies"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each backend has different requirements. In this guide we’ll use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/DefaultBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" which uses "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/AppKitBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" on macOS, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/GtkBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" on Linux, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/WinUIBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" on Windows, and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/UIKitBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" on iOS\/tvOS. Click through the backend relevant to your machine for detailed installation requirements. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/AppKitBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/UIKitBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" have no system dependencies."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Using-Swift-Bundlers-SwiftCrossUI-template","type":"heading","text":"Using Swift Bundler’s SwiftCrossUI template"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Bundler provides many built-in templates; we’ll use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftCrossUI"},{"type":"text","text":" template. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftCrossUI"},{"type":"text","text":" template uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultBackend"},{"type":"text","text":" to select the most appropriate backend at compile time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["swift bundler create HelloWorld --template SwiftCrossUI","cd HelloWorld"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Running-your-app","type":"heading","text":"Running your app"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Running your new app with Swift Bundler is as simple as it gets!"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["swift bundler run"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On macOS you can provide the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--device <device_name_or_id>"},{"type":"text","text":" option to run the app on a connected iOS or tvOS device, or the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--simulator <simulator_name_or_id>"},{"type":"text","text":" option to run the app in a simulator."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["# You can use any substring of the target device name. For example,","# \"iPhone\" matches any device connected with \"iPhone\" in its name.","swift bundler run --device \"iPhone\"","swift bundler run --simulator \"iPhone 15\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Making-a-change","type":"heading","text":"Making a change"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Open ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sources\/HelloWorld\/HelloWorldApp.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in an editor of your choosing. Change ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"Hello, World!\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"Hello, Earth!\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Repeat the previous step to verify that your changes get reflected.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"All-done","type":"heading","text":"All done"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You’re good to go! If you make something cool with SwiftCrossUI let us know so we can add your project to our showcase once the SwiftCrossUI website is up and running!"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Quick-start"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftcrossui\/quick-start"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Creating a cross-platform SwiftCrossUI app with Swift Bundler.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Setting-up-a-development-environment","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Setting-up-a-virtual-development-environment","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Examples","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Hot-reloading"],"title":"Getting Started","anchor":"Getting-Started","gene